  "limitations": [
    "Scratch checks compile the same original five source bodies sequentially or concatenated once, in the pinned Lake environment. They do not run all ordinary Lake build facets. Split copies import already validated predecessor artifacts; merged proofs have preceding definitions physically in their file.",
    "The three-pair confirmation alternates arm order split/merged, merged/split, split/merged and uses ordinary warm filesystem caches. These medians have only three samples per arm, not a population-level performance guarantee.",
    "The first fixed single-pair pilot is kept separate from the three-pair confirmation, rather than pooled into its medians.",
    "Reported ru_maxrss comes from os.wait4 child usage and is compared as maximum within each sequential arm, never summed across modules. It is not an aggregate simultaneous process-tree or system-memory peak.",
    "The import-only invocation includes startup, environment import, artifact output and shutdown; its elapsed time is evidence of large fixed overhead, not a pure import/tactic timing decomposition.",
    "The ordinary Lake pair validates a real target rebuild (5 modules versus 1). It is a single paired target measurement, not a full-project before/after benchmark.",
    "The subsequent broad19 groups include more proof bodies per final target, and the Core split changes inherited imports. Final target timings therefore measure the combined architecture on a broader workload than the initial five-file pilot.",
    "The current full build is not a matched repeat of the R1911 rebuild: changed file sets, grouping, dependency footprints and concurrency differ. Do not derive a whole-build speed ratio from their wall times or sum parallel job times."
  ],
